"AVCME" means the Minecraft mod AVCME in every version and form in which cptgummiball
publishes it: the jar files, the compiled code in them, textures, models, icons, sounds, texts,
language files, data files and documentation, and the AVCME API files (section 5).

1. Ownership
   AVCME is the property of cptgummiball. This license gives you limited rights to use it. It
   does not transfer any ownership, copyright or other rights. All rights not expressly granted
   here are reserved.

2. What you may do
   a) Download AVCME from its official pages (Modrinth, CurseForge, and the releases of
      https://github.com/CptGummiball/AVCME).
   b) Use AVCME to play Minecraft: in singleplayer, and on your own or any other server.
   c) Show AVCME in videos, streams, screenshots, reviews and guides.

3. Modpacks
   You may include AVCME in modpacks, public or private, free or paid, and distribute it as part
   of such a modpack, but only in its original, unmodified state: the jar files exactly as
   cptgummiball published them, not renamed in content, not repackaged, not altered in any way.
   Where the modpack platform can link to the official download instead of copying the file,
   linking is preferred.

4. What you may not do
   Unless cptgummiball has given you written permission, you may not:
   a) modify, adapt, translate, patch or otherwise change AVCME or any part of it, or create
      works derived from it, including modified jar files, forks, ports and re-textures;
   b) decompile, disassemble, deobfuscate or otherwise reverse engineer AVCME, or attempt to
      obtain its source code, except where and only to the extent that applicable law expressly
      allows this despite this restriction;
   c) upload, mirror or distribute AVCME anywhere other than as part of a modpack under
      section 3, or offer it as your own work;
   d) use the textures, models, icons, sounds or texts of AVCME in other projects;
   e) remove or change this license or any copyright notice.

5. AVCME API
   cptgummiball publishes an API for other mods: the Java package dev.cptgummiball.avcme.api (provided as a
   separate API jar with its documentation) and the documented integration classes, if any. You
   may use the API jar, the documentation and the official AVCME jar files as compile-only
   dependencies to develop, compile and distribute your own mods that work together with
   AVCME. Your mod may reference these classes, but must not contain the API classes or
   any other part of AVCME; players install AVCME separately. The API may not be
   modified or redistributed on its own. Sections 1 and 4 apply to the API in all other respects.

